Oru chinna correction bro!

escapeHtml function-kku appuram already oru script close aagi irukkum (illana adhu JavaScript kulla varum). JavaScript kulla direct-ah <script> tag podakoodadhu.

Pazhaya <script> tag mudinja appuram idhai podanum. Exact-ah indha maadhiri irukannum:

JavaScript
    // Safety string escaping for user notes
    function escapeHtml(str) {
      if (!str) return '';
      return str.replace(/[&<>"']/g, function(m) {
        return {
          '&': '&amp;',
          '<': '&lt;',
          '>': '&gt;',
          '"': '&quot;',
          "'": '&#039;'
        }[m];
      });
    }

    // Service Worker registration (direct-a script kulla)
    if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) {
      navigator.serviceWorker.register('./sw.js');
    }
  </script>
</body>
</html>
Andha extra <script> tag theva illa, direct-ah escapeHtml function mudinja udane if ('serviceWorker' in navigator) ... nu paste pannitu kadaisila </script> </body> </html> irukkura maadhiri paathukonga!

